<title>JAPAN: Japan Sept aluminium imports up 27.0 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Japan Sept aluminium imports up 27.0 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's refined aluminium imports in September were 249,208 tonnes, up 27.0 percent from 196,227 tonnes in the same month a year earlier, Finance Ministry statistics released on Tuesday showed.</p>
<p>The breakdown was as follows (on a customs-cleared basis, in tonnes):</p>
<p>		  Sept 96	    Aug 96     Sept 95</p>
<p> Total	  249,208	   237,155     196,227</p>
<p>Major suppliers:</p>
<p> Brazil	  54,148	    50,566	30,373</p>
<p> Russia	  42,765	    38,475	38,792</p>
<p> Australia     32,561	    34,589	31,995</p>
<p> U.S.	    14,357	    21,550	23,279</p>
<p>Refined aluminium imports in the first nine months of 1996 were 2,062,182 tonnes, off 4.3 percent from 2,155,474 tonnes in the same period last year.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Commodities desk (81-3 3432 6179)</p>
</text>
